amux add — add an agent to a workgroup

usage: amux add <workgroup> ["<task>"] [flags]

Adds a member agent within the workgroup's repos and gives it <task> as its
first prompt. With only <workgroup>, pick the agent's settings interactively
(needs a terminal). Members run as tasks; --interactive makes this one
interactive (driven turn by turn, closed by you).

flags:
  --repo <name>        (repeatable) the agent's repos, within the workgroup's (repeat, or give a comma list)
  --harness <harness>  the agent's harness: claude | codex (default: claude)
  --model <model>      the agent's model (default: the harness's default)
  --interactive        advanced: an interactive agent instead of a task

examples:
  amux add 9c1b "write the migration" --repo api
  amux add 9c1b
